{
  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 + multiprofile + avgpool is the strongest RNA-only setup (0.650-0.653). The only multimodal test (config_030, resnet50, concat) scored 0.632, slightly *below* the RNA-only baseline (0.650), and image-only with resnet50 was very poor (0.208). This raises a critical uncertainty: is the image modality fundamentally unhelpful, or was resnet50 simply too weak an encoder to contribute useful signal? Question: config_036 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) isolates the image-encoder variable by swapping resnet50 → ViT-L while holding all other settings identical to config_030. If ViT-L multimodal exceeds the RNA-only baseline, it confirms the image modality is useful and justifies further multimodal exploration (fusion strategy, transformer aggregation). If it still underperforms RNA-only, it strongly indicates images are not contributing and remaining budget should focus on RNA-only refinements. This is the highest-information experiment under the limited budget because the answer directly determines the direction of all subsequent experiments."
}

